$$2x - 3y = -2$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$-5$"},{"key":"B","text":"$4$"},{"key":"C","text":"$5$"},{"key":"D","text":"$7$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'C', NULL, E'Adding the two equations eliminates $y$: $(5x + 3y) + (2x - 3y) = 37 + (-2)$, giving $7x = 35$, so $x = 5$. The value $-5$ results from a sign error when dividing. The value $4$ is actually the $y$-value of the solution (substituting $x = 5$ into the first equation gives $25 + 3y = 37$, so $y = 4$), which answers the wrong question. The value $7$ could arise from dividing $35$ by $5$ instead of $7$.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"misread_question"},"C":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"arithmetic_slip"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 50, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);





































